cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Transcendental crossing heights in two theta prime races"
abstract: "Every nonzero algebraic target of the normalized doubling move is attained only at transcendental starts. A finite knot matrix classifies all algebraic linear relations among readings of the two hosts at sufficiently large algebraic starts. At algebraic starts, the six readings at scales 1, √2 and 2 have rank seven with 1 exactly above the threshold 79√2/8."
